#
# SEP-0007 (defensible EXISTS) fixture for `:existsGraphVariableCorrelated`. This
# file is loaded TWICE by the harness — once untagged (`qt:data`, into the default
# graph) and once tagged with its own file IRI (`qt:graphData`), exactly like the
# vendored `w3c-sparql11/exists/exists-graph-variable` case this fixture follows
# byte-for-byte. `<>` self-references the file's own graph IRI, so `:s1 :p <>`
# puts a pointer to this very named graph in the default graph, and `:a1 :q :b1`
# becomes visible inside `GRAPH ?g { … }` once `?g` is bound to that pointer — the
# definition-path Graph-substitution shape (`GraphPattern::Graph(Var, ·)` in
# `crate::enf`'s `Replace` sites).
@prefix : <https://example.org/exists#> .

:s1 :p <> .
:a1 :q :b1 .
